{
  "dom_id": "step-q556465",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Estimate the value of $\\sqrt{28},$ rounded to $1$ decimal place.\n\n$\\sqrt{28}≈$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To estimate $\\sqrt{28},$ we first find the two perfect squares closest to $28.$\n\nThe closest perfect squares are $25={5}^{2}$ and $36={6}^{2}.$\n\nSince $25<28<36,$ we know that the square root of $28$ lies between $5$ and $6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14221205/assets/9f16093fe61b05142060e1dcc36cf824ec664b271499d24758831a6bc53757ac.png)\n\nSince $28$ lies between $25$ and $36,$ we expect $\\sqrt{28}$ to lie between $5$ and $6.$\n\nLet's test decimals near the middle by squaring them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5.2}^{2} & =27.04 \\\\ {5.3}^{2} & =28.09\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that $28$ lies between $27.04$ and $28.09,$ so $5.2<\\sqrt{28}<5.3.$\n\nNext, we determine which value is closer to $28:$\n\n- The distance from $28$ to ${5.2}^{2}$ is $28-27.04=0.96.$\n\n- The distance from $28$ to ${5.3}^{2}$ is $28.09-28=0.09.$\n\nSince $28$ is much closer to $28.09,$ $\\sqrt{28}$ is closer to $5.3.$\n\nTherefore, rounded to $1$ decimal place, $\\sqrt{28}≈5.3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
